From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 22:15:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/mediatek: Unbind the display stub driver last

mtk_ddp_comp_init() keeps the register mapping of the postmask and
dither units in their devices' drvdata, and the stub driver binds those
devices. platform_unregister_drivers() unbinds in reverse order, so
unloading the module unbound the stub first, the driver core cleared the
drvdata, and the CRTC disable that follows in mtk_drm_unbind() oopsed in
mtk_postmask_stop() (seen on the Minimal Phone MP01, MT6789).

Register the stub first, so that it is unbound after the components that
use its devices.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_drv.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_drv.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_drv.c
@@ -1357,7 +1357,12 @@
 	},
 };
 
+/*
+ * The stub goes first, so that it is unbound last: unbinding it clears the
+ * drvdata that mtk_ddp_comp_init() keeps on its devices.
+ */
 static struct platform_driver * const mtk_drm_drivers[] = {
+	&mtk_disp_stub_driver,
 	&mtk_disp_aal_driver,
 	&mtk_disp_ccorr_driver,
 	&mtk_disp_color_driver,
@@ -1372,7 +1377,6 @@
 	&mtk_ethdr_driver,
 	&mtk_mdp_rdma_driver,
 	&mtk_padding_driver,
-	&mtk_disp_stub_driver,
 };
 
 static int __init mtk_drm_init(void)
